Quoting  archmage84  <archmage84@live.com>:
>I should probably mention a few things about my playing style:
>1. I play human female characters exclusively.

This is not "playing style". This is a self-imposed challenge. That's
fine; I play with self-imposed challenges too. But if your primary
objective is to ascend you should waive this rule and play the most
effective race for any given class.

>3. I know all the stuff about resistances, the trinity of win
>(Reflection, MR and MC), engrave-IDing wands, price-IDing most things,

Coo, I can't be arsed to price-ID most things. ID, lamps, water,
spellbooks, that's about my limit.

>10. Artifacts I want to get are in this order:
> a) Eyes of the Overworld - wish
> b) Greyswandir - wish
> c) PYEC - wish
> d) Mjollnir - sacrifest
> e) Orb of Fate - quest

Wishing for other people's Quest artifacts is pretty weak (yeah, here's
another self-imposed challenge) and definitely quite unnecessary. By the
time you reach the Castle you will already expect to have at least Mojo
and the Orb; you would need a lot of wishes to complete that shopping
list because of the way the chance of getting artifacts drops off, and the
Castle wand would better be used on the non-artifact items you need.

There's no use in having this kind of impossible wishlist.

> a - the blessed +7 Grayswandir (weapon in hand)
> b - a blessed +7 silver saber (wielded in other hand)
> Armour
> c - a +5 Hawaiian shirt
> d - a +5 silver dragon scale mail
> e - a +5 oilskin cloak
> d - a +5 gauntlets of power
> e - a +5 helm of telepathy
> f - a +5 boots of speed

The most obvious thing wrong with this list is that there's no magic
resistance in it, remembering that the idea that you will wish for
Grayswandir _and_ the Eyes is basically implausible.

The oilskin cloak is a special-use item. It should not be part of your
regular kit. A CoMR would fill the resistance hole - or, if you fill it
elsewhere, a CoDisplacement would be better.

> Rings
> g - a blessed ring of slow digestion (worn on right hand)
> h - a blessed ring of conflict
> i - a blessed +x ring of increase damage (worn on left hand)
> j - a blessed +x ring of increase damage

Entirely pointless. Food is not in short supply in the endgame, and your
twoweapon combination will do ludicrous damage even with a more plausible
primary weapon. Free action should be top of the rings list.
